# CODEOWNERS
#
# Template repo: every change needs review from the framework owners
# (Engineering Lead and Technical PO). GitHub accepts any ONE code owner's approval,
# so the "both approve" rule also needs the branch ruleset in docs/framework/GOVERNANCE.md.
#
# In a project repo, /start-project replaces the owners below with the project's owners.
# Use GitHub handles (@user) or teams (@org/team). Later rules override earlier ones.

# Default owners for everything
*                                             <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>

# Framework-owned paths (keep in sync with ownership.framework_owned in .ai-framework.yml)
/.github/skills/                              <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
/.github/agents/                              <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
/.github/copilot-instructions.md              <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
/.github/instructions/catalogue/              <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/framework-change.md   <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
/framework/                                   <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
/docs/framework/                              <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
/.harness/                                    <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>

# Governance files (project-owned, but changes still need owner review)
/.ai-framework.yml                            <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
/.github/CODEOWNERS                           <FILL:@engineering-lead> <FILL:@technical-po>
